  "worked_solution": "To compute the value of an observation $x$ which yields a given $z$-score in a data set with mean $\\overset{\u2015}{x}$ and standard deviation $\\sigma ,$ we can use the following formula:\n\n$$\nx=\\overset{\u2015}{x}+z\\cdot \\sigma \n$$\n\nSubstituting $\\overset{\u2015}{x}=64.3,$ $z=-1,$ and $\\sigma =5.25$ into the formula, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & =\\overset{\u2015}{x}+z\\cdot \\sigma  \\\\  & =64.3+(-1)\\cdot 5.25 \\\\  & =64.3-5.25 \\\\  & =59.05.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nTherefore, the minimum passing score is $59.05%.$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
